# Describing people in Russian: похо́ж на па́пу
subtitle: "Describe people in Russian: высо́кий or ни́зкий, голубы́е глаза́ and тёмные во́лосы, a beard, and who they look like: он похо́ж на па́пу."
tags: ["russian","describing people","appearance","похож на","russian vocabulary"]
teaches: ["vocabulary/looks"]
thumb: "band \"Who do you look like?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"The biggest in Russian: са́мый большо́й","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/82-russian-superlative.cast"}

